The attached image displays confocal microscopy results illustrating the uptake of fluorescently labeled Nano-11 nanoparticles and ovalbumin (OVA) by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). The top row shows efficient internalization of Nano-11 (red). The middle row indicates minimal uptake of soluble OVA (green). The bottom row demonstrates a significantly enhanced uptake of OVA when adsorbed to Nano-11, with clear colocalization of Nano-11 (red) and OVA (green) within the BMDCs. This visually confirms that Nano-11 facilitates the delivery of negatively charged antigens to dendritic cells, a key mechanism for its adjuvant effect.